# secrets — the Gemini API keys live here. Never commit this.
.env
*.key

# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# os
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Icon working files. The generated 2048px JPEGs and rejected takes are worth keeping
# locally but they are ~29 MB and nothing on the site loads them — only the finished
# PNGs under assets/icons/ ship.
docs/design/reference/icon-drafts/
docs/design/*.pdf

# Properly keyed and unpremultiplied versions of the seven format icons, made to fix
# assets/icons/formats/*-alpha.png shipping fully opaque despite the name — see
# docs/attack/FIX-10.md. The finished result is already copied to assets/icons/formats/;
# this is the working copy, worth keeping locally but not worth a second copy in git.
docs/design/scratch-icons/

# Generated from data/*.json by scripts/build-data-js.py. Committing both means every
# data change shows up as two diffs, one of them unreadable minified JSON.
# Run ./build.sh after cloning.
data/items.js
data/paths.js
data/search-keywords.js
data/publisher-marks.js
data/picks.js

# --- Deliberately NOT ignored, so nobody adds them later --------------------
#
# docs/FIX-THESE*.md and docs/attack/FIX-*.md are the briefs Morteza wrote for each
# round of work. They are tracked on purpose: docs/attack/RUN-LOG.md records what was
# done and these record what was asked, and one without the other is half a record.
# They arrived in git by accident - a `git add -A` in commit 87a7c24 swept up nine
# untracked files under a commit message about something else - and were then reviewed
# and kept rather than removed, because rewriting pushed history costs more than the
# tidiness is worth.
#
# .claude/launch.json is tracked for the same kind of reason: it is how anyone cloning
# this starts the dev server, and it holds nothing private.
#
# The real fix was not a gitignore entry. It was to stop staging with `git add -A` and
# name the paths instead, which is what every commit since does.
